{
  "title": "Dua Faraj (Release from Grief) يَا عِمَادَ مَنْ لَا عِمَادَ لَهُ",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Shaykh al-Kaf’ami, in al-Balad al-Ameen, has mentioned a supplicatory prayer that is reported from Imam Ali Ameer al-Momineen (a.s.) saying that no grief-stricken, worried, depressed, distressed, or aggrieved person recites it but that Almighty Allah will certainly take the edge off him. This supplication is as follows:\nيَا عِمَادَ مَنْ لَا عِمَادَ لَهٗ\nYAA E’MAADA MAN LAA E’MAADA LAHU\nO Pillar of the one who has no pillar! \nوَ يَا ذُخْرَ مَنْ لَا ذُخْرَ لَهٗ\nWA YAA ZUKHRA MAN LAA ZUKHRA LAHU \nO Treasure of the one who has no treasure! \nوَيَا سَنَدَ مَنْ لَا سَنَدَ لَهٗ\nWA YAA SANADA MAN LAA SANADA LAHU \nO Support of the one who has no support! \nوَ يَا حِرْزَ مَنْ لَا حِرْزَ لَهٗ\nWA YAA HIRZA MAN LAA HIRZA LAHU \nO Sanctuary of the one who has no sanctuary! \nوَ يَا غِيَاثَ مَنْ لَا غِيَاثَ لَهٗ\nWA YAA GHEYAASA MAN LAA GHEYAASA LAHU\nO Helper of the one who has no helper! \nوَ يَا كَنْزَ مَنْ لَا كَنْزَ لَهٗ\nWA YAA KANZA MAN LAA KANZA LAHU \nO Storehouse of the one who has no storehouse! \nوَ يَا عِزَّ مَنْ لَا عِزَّ لَهٗ\nWA YAA I’ZZA MAN LAA I’ZZA LAHU\nO Might of the one who has no might!\nيَا كَرِيْمَ الْعَفْوِ يَا حَسَنَ التَّجَاوُزِ\nYAA KAREEMAL A’FWE YAA HASANAT TAJAAWOZE\nO Noble in forgiveness! O Beautiful in forbearance! \nيَا عَوْنَ الضُّعَفاۤءِ يَا كَنْزَ الْفُقَرَاۤءِ\nYAA A’WNAZ ZO-A’FAAA-E’ YAA KANZAL FOQARAAA-E\nO Helper of the weak! O Wealth of the poor! \nيَا عَظِيْمَ الرَّجَاۤءِ يَا مُنْقِذَ الْغَرْقٰى\nYAA A’ZEEMAR RAJAAA-E YAA MUNQEZAL GHARQAA \nO Sublime Object of hope! O Deliverer of the drowning! \nيَا مُنْجِىَ الْهَلْكٰى يَا مُحْسِنُ\nYAA MUNJEYAL HALKAA YAA MOHSENO\nO Savior of the perishing! O Beneficent! \nيَا مُجْمِلُ يَا مُنْعِمُ يَا مُفْضِلُ\nYAA MUJMELO YAA MUN-E’MO YAA MUFZELO\nO Gracious! O Bestower of blessings! O Giver of bounty!\nاَنْتَ الَّذِىْ سَجَدَ لَكَ سَوَادُ اللَّيْلِ وَ نُوْرُ النَّهَارِ\nANTAL LAZEE SAJADA LAKA SAWAADUL LAYLE WA NOORUN NAHAARE\nYou are the One before whom bows the darkness of the night, the light of the day, \nوَ ضَوْءُ الْقَمَرِ وَ شُعَاعُ الشَّمْسِ\nWA ZAW-UL QAMARE WA SHO-A’A-USH SHAMSE\nthe radiance of the moon, the rays of the sun, \nوَحَفِيْفُ الشَّجَرِ وَ دَوِىُّ الْمَاۤءِ\nWA HAFEEFUSH SHAJARE WA DAWIYYUL MAAA-E\nthe rustling of the trees, and the murmuring of the water!\nيَا اَللهُ يَا اَللهُ يَا اَللهُ\nYAA ALLAAHO YAA ALLAAHO YAA ALLAAHO \nO Allah! O Allah! O Allah! \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ وَحْدَكَ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَكَ\nLAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA WAHD-AKA LAA SHAREEKA LAKA \nThere is no god except You, alone, without any partner. \nيَا رَبَّاهُ يَا اَللهُ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nYAA RABBAAHO YAA ALLAAHO SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADINW\nO Lord! O Allah! Bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, \nوَّ افْعَلْ بِنَا مَا اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ.\nWAF-A’L BENAA MAA ANTA AHLOHU.\nand deal with us according to what befits You.\nYou may then mention your personal needs.\nIt is worth mentioning that the following supplicatory prayer is reported from Imam Muhammad al-Jawad(a.s.) who said that if it is recited regularly, it achieves relief and releases from grief and ordeals:\nيَا مَنْ يَّكْفِىْ مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّلَا يَكْفِىْ مِنْهُ شَىْءٌ اِكْفِنِىْ مَاۤ اَهَمَّنِىْ\nYAA MAY YAKFEE MIN KULLE SHAY-IW WA LAA YAKFEE MINHO SHAY-UN IKFENEE MAA AHAMMANEE.\nO One who suffices against all things, while nothing can suffice against Him! Suffice me in that which worries and distresses me."
}
